       Arguments:

       "mode: COLOMode"
           report COLO mode when COLO exited.

       "reason: COLOExitReason"
           describes the reason for the COLO exit.

       Since: 3.1

       Example:

               <- { "timestamp": {"seconds": 2032141960, "microseconds": 417172},
                    "event": "COLO_EXIT", "data": {"mode": "primary", "reason": "request" } }

       COLOExitReason (Enum)

       The reason for a COLO exit

       Values:

       "none"
           no failover has ever happened. This can't occur in the COLO_EXIT event, only in the result of query-colo-status.

       "request"
           COLO exit is due to an external request

       "error"
           COLO exit is due to an internal error

       Since: 3.1

       x-colo-lost-heartbeat  (Command) Tell qemu that heartbeat is lost, request it to do takeover procedures.  If this command is sent to the PVM, the Primary side will exit COLO
       mode.  If sent to the Secondary, the Secondary side will run failover work, then takes over server operation to become the service VM.

       Since: 2.8

       Example:

               -> { "execute": "x-colo-lost-heartbeat" }
               <- { "return": {} }

       migrate_cancel  (Command) Cancel the current executing migration process.

       Returns: nothing on success

       Notes: This command succeeds even if there is no migration process running.

       Since: 0.14.0

       Example:

               -> { "execute": "migrate_cancel" }
               <- { "return": {} }

